Embedded CLDR data
------------------
The file `data/cldr47.json` and the generated port tables derived from it
(`rust/src/data.rs`, `typescript/src/data.ts`, `python/lomboklocale/_data.py`,
`go/data.go`, `php/src/Data.php`) embed a subset of the Unicode Common
Locale Data Repository (CLDR), release 47.0.0, distributed by Unicode as the
`cldr-json` package (tag `47.0.0`, https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json).

That subset is limited to what the library actually uses:

- number, percent and currency symbols and patterns for 28 locales
  (`en`, `en-GB`, `en-IN`, `id`, `ms`, `jv`, `su`, `de`, `fr`, `es`, `pt`,
  `pt-PT`, `it`, `nl`, `ru`, `uk`, `pl`, `tr`, `ar`, `hi`, `zh`, `zh-Hant`,
  `ja`, `ko`, `vi`, `th`, `sv`, `cy`);
- the default fraction digits of 14 currencies (ISO 4217: USD, EUR, GBP, JPY,
  CNY, IDR, MYR, SGD, INR, KRW, SAR, AUD, THB, VND);
- date patterns and the format-context month, day and era names of the same
  28 locales;
- cardinal plural rules for 219 locales and ordinal rules for 104 locales.

The data was extracted by `scripts/extract_cldr.py` and embedded into each
port by `scripts/gen_ports.py`; the regeneration is checked in CI
(`python3 scripts/gen_ports.py --check`). No other CLDR content is included,
and nothing is fetched at runtime.

